<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Drop-In Respite &mdash; Legacy Home &amp; Respite Care Foundation</title>
<meta name="description" content="Drop-in respite for dementia caregivers in Milwaukee — supervised, engaging, non-medical activities for your loved one while you take time for yourself.">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:wght@500;600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>


{% set active_page = 'drop-in-respite' %}
{% include '_header.html.j2' %}

{#
  Same hero treatment as the home page: Shanelle's own footage behind the copy, gradient
  underneath so the hero still reads if the video fails or reduced-motion is set. Source is
  720x1280 portrait phone video, so it is inset rather than stretched - see the .hero.has-video
  rules in styles.css for why. Page content: Shanelle's Nov 3 rebuild request.
#}
<section class="hero has-video">
  <video class="hero-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" data-playback-rate="0.75"
         poster="media/respite-poster.jpg" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
    <source src="media/respite.webm" type="video/webm">
    <source src="media/respite.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  </video>
  <div class="container pos-rel-z2">
    <p class="eyebrow text-sand-light"><a class="text-sand-light" href="programs-events.html">Programs &amp; Events</a></p>
    <h1>Drop-In Respite Program</h1>
    <p class="lede">A Break for You. Meaningful Moments for Your Loved One.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="#how-it-works" class="btn btn-outline-light">How it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="about-respite">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="respite-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="muted mb-16">Everyone deserves an opportunity to take a break, especially those caring for someone living with dementia.</p>
        <p class="muted mb-16">Our free Drop-In Respite program offers caregivers time for themselves while their loved ones enjoy meaningful activities, social connection, and compassionate support in a welcoming environment.</p>
        <p class="muted mb-16">Whether you need to run errands, attend appointments, or simply recharge, we're here to help.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card respite-details">
        <h2 class="fs-18-mb-14">Program Details</h2>
        <dl class="respite-details-list">
          <dt>When</dt><dd>Every Third Thursday of the Month</dd>
          <dt>Time</dt><dd>10:00 AM &ndash; 2:00 PM</dd>
          <dt>Where</dt><dd>Ebenezer Ministry &amp; Family Worship Center</dd>
          <dt>Address</dt><dd><address>3132 N. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Drive<br>Milwaukee, WI 53212</address></dd>
          <dt>Cost</dt><dd><strong>FREE</strong></dd>
        </dl>
        <a href="#sessions" class="btn btn-coral w-100">Register for Free Respite</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sand" id="different">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>What Makes Our Respite Different?</h2></div>
    <p class="muted measure-640 mb-16">We believe respite should be more than supervision. It should be a meaningful experience for the person living with dementia, too.</p>
    <p class="muted measure-640 mb-16">Our program uses a <strong>person-centered approach</strong>, recognizing each individual's unique interests, abilities, preferences, and life experiences.</p>
    <div class="card-grid grid-autofit-240 mt-24">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">&#127925;</div>
        <h3>Meaningful Engagement</h3>
        <p>Music, creative activities, games, conversation, and opportunities for social connection.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">&#129505;</div>
        <h3>Person-Centered Care</h3>
        <p>Activities and interactions adapted to each participant's interests, strengths, and abilities.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">&#129309;</div>
        <h3>Compassionate Support</h3>
        <p>Dementia-trained team members providing supervision and non-medical support in a welcoming environment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9749;</div>
        <h3>Time for Caregivers</h3>
        <p>An opportunity to rest, attend appointments, run errands, or focus on personal well-being.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="sessions">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Upcoming Respite Sessions</h2></div>
    <p class="muted measure-640">Every third Thursday, 10 AM &ndash; 2 PM, at Ebenezer Ministry &amp; Family Worship Center.</p>
    <p class="respite-note"><em>Advance registration is requested. Participation is based on individual support needs and available capacity.</em></p>
    {#
      Live sessions: a published Staff-console event whose title starts with "Drop-In Respite"
      replaces the planned card for its own date, with its own Register button. Other planned
      dates stay, with a contact route instead of a Register button that could not save anything.
    #}
    <div class="card-grid grid-autofit-240 mt-24" id="liveEventsGrid" data-event-time-zone="America/Chicago"
         data-event-title-prefix="Drop-In Respite" data-event-badge="Drop-In Respite"
         data-keep-when-empty aria-live="polite">
{%- for iso, d in [("2026-11-19", "Thursday, November 19, 2026"), ("2026-12-17", "Thursday, December 17, 2026"), ("2027-01-21", "Thursday, January 21, 2027"), ("2027-02-18", "Thursday, February 18, 2027")] %}
      <div class="card event-card" data-planned-date="{{ iso }}">
        <div class="flex-1">
          <span class="badge badge-plum">Drop-In Respite</span>
          <h3 class="fs-19-m-8-0-4">{{ d }}</h3>
          <p class="event-meta">10 AM &ndash; 2 PM &middot; Ebenezer Ministry &amp; Family Worship Center</p>
          <p class="small muted">Online registration for this date opens soon. Contact us to save a spot.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" href="about.html#contact">Contact us to register</a>
        </div>
      </div>
{%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sand" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>How It Works</h2></div>
    <ol class="card-grid grid-autofit-240 respite-steps">
      <li class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
        <h3>Register</h3>
        <p>Select an upcoming respite date and complete the registration form.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
        <h3>Connect With Our Team</h3>
        <p>For first-time participants, our team will follow up to learn more about your loved one's needs, preferences, and how we can best support them.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
        <h3>Take Some Time for Yourself</h3>
        <p>Once participation is confirmed, your loved one can enjoy meaningful activities and companionship while you take time for yourself.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="faith-community">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Bring Respite to Your Faith Community</h2></div>
    <p class="muted measure-640 mb-16">Faith communities have long been places of connection, compassion, and care. We believe they can also play an important role in supporting families navigating dementia.</p>
    <p class="muted measure-640 mb-16">Legacy partners with faith communities to expand access to respite through caregiver education, dementia training, and collaborative program development.</p>
    <p class="muted measure-640 mb-16">Together, we can create welcoming spaces where caregivers receive support and individuals living with dementia experience meaningful engagement.</p>
    <div class="btn-row mt-24">
      <a href="get-involved.html#partner" class="btn btn-coral">Interested in Bringing Respite to Your Faith Community?</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# Same registration modal as the Events page; tests keep the two identical. #}
<!-- Registration modal -->
<div class="modal-overlay" id="registerModal">
  <div class="modal">
    <button class="modal-close" data-action="close-register">✕</button>
    <h3 id="regTitle">Register</h3>
    <p class="sub">One quick form — no re-typing your details every time.</p>
    <form id="regForm" data-action="submit-register">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="regName">Your name</label>
        <input id="regName" type="text" placeholder="e.g., Maria Gonzalez" required>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="regEmail">Email</label>
        <input id="regEmail" type="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="regRole">I am a…</label>
        <select id="regRole">
          <option>Family caregiver</option>
          <option>Professional caregiver</option>
          <option>Volunteer</option>
          <option>Community member</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <p class="privacy-line">By registering, you consent to Legacy using these details to create or update your caregiver record, manage attendance, and send event follow-up. Please do not include medical record numbers or emergency details.</p>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-coral w-100">Complete registration</button>
      <div class="success-note" id="regSuccess" data-intake-success role="status" aria-live="polite">✓ Registration received — thank you.</div>
      <div class="error-note" data-intake-error role="alert" aria-live="assertive"></div>
      <div class="routing-note" id="regRouting" data-intake-routing>Behind the scenes: this registration routed into the caregiver record — profile matched, attendance list updated, follow-up queued for staff.</div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

{% include '_footer.html.j2' %}

<script src="app.js"></script>
<script src="nav-v2.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
